<article class="env-remark" id="088M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/088M">Remark <span data-tag="088M">70.13.2</span>.</a> We have seen in Examples, Section <a href="/tag/088V" data-tag="088V">110.29</a> that Lemma <a href="/tag/088L" data-tag="088L">70.13.1</a> does not hold if we drop the assumption that $X$ be locally separated. This raises the question: Does Lemma <a href="/tag/088L" data-tag="088L">70.13.1</a> hold if we drop the assumption that $X$ be quasi-separated? If you know the answer, please email <a href="mailto:stacks.project@gmail.com">stacks.project@gmail.com</a>. </p>
